          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Uprisings and Death</strong><br>\nGaddafi's regime was eventually challenged by uprisings during the Arab Spring. In 2011, after a civil war and international military intervention, he was captured and killed by rebel forces, bringing an abrupt end to his 42-year rule.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Gaddafi's Legacy</strong><br>\nGaddafi's legacy remains contentious, characterized by his unique ideology, repressive domestic policies, and the dramatic fall from power, which left a power vacuum and ongoing instability in Libya.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
